00:02:14.662 --> 00:02:16.322
"Aladdin," the film had just come out

00:02:16.322 --> 00:02:17.677
and there's a tiger named Raja.

00:02:17.677 --> 00:02:19.633
And I was also born in
the year of the tiger.

00:02:19.633 --> 00:02:20.573
So it all kind of went together.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.193
- Oh, that was just kind of meant to be.

00:02:22.193 --> 00:02:23.026
(audience clapping)

00:02:23.026 --> 00:02:23.859
I love that.

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:27.187
That reminds me of John Legend,
his last name and legend.

00:02:27.187 --> 00:02:28.462
Right? He just was like, I'm a legend.

00:02:28.462 --> 00:02:29.377
I'm gonna call myself a legend.

00:02:29.377 --> 00:02:30.210
- [Yvie] Really?

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.043
- I know!

00:02:31.043 --> 00:02:31.876
- Oh!

00:02:31.876 --> 00:02:32.709
- [Kelly] It's Stevens!

00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:33.542
- [Monet] Oh, wow!

00:02:33.542 --> 00:02:34.375
- [Kelly] I was like,

00:02:34.375 --> 00:02:35.208
but I love that.

00:02:35.208 --> 00:02:36.721
He was like, naw. Legend.

00:02:36.721 --> 00:02:37.687
(queens laughing)

00:02:37.687 --> 00:02:40.037
Yeah. And I love that you
were like, king. This bit.

00:02:40.037 --> 00:02:40.870
I like it.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.703
I like it.

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:42.953
I, I should have picked a cooler name.

00:02:42.953 --> 00:02:44.167
(queens laughing)

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:46.657
So, so how did you, how
did you all get into drag?

00:02:46.657 --> 00:02:48.197
Raja, I'll start with you.

00:02:48.197 --> 00:02:50.567
- I'm probably here on this panel,

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.122
I've been doing it the longest.

00:02:52.122 --> 00:02:54.187
And I think it, it was, you
know, it's been 30 years

00:02:54.187 --> 00:02:56.461
since I started doing
drag for the first time.

00:02:56.461 --> 00:02:57.294
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:57.294 --> 00:02:59.397
- [Raja] And at that time
it was, it was irreverent.

00:02:59.397 --> 00:03:00.242
It was rebellion.

00:03:00.242 --> 00:03:01.757
And it was just kind of, you know,

00:03:01.757 --> 00:03:03.422
it was just something to do-

00:03:03.422 --> 00:03:04.255
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:04.255 --> 00:03:05.564
- just to kind of make my parents little-

00:03:05.564 --> 00:03:06.567
- [Kelly] It's very creative.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:07.400
(Raja laughing)

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.636
I mean, Lord, it's so cool.

00:03:08.636 --> 00:03:10.456
But Shea, how about you?

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.982
- It was like, kind of an accident.

00:03:12.982 --> 00:03:14.735
I went to school for theater

00:03:14.735 --> 00:03:17.396
and I was supposed to
be dancing in the chorus

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.041
for this all black burlesque review

00:03:19.041 --> 00:03:20.682
called "Jeezy's Juke Joint,"

00:03:20.682 --> 00:03:22.442
and my good friend, Jeez Louise,

00:03:22.442 --> 00:03:25.035
she sent out the email
to everybody in the cast

00:03:25.035 --> 00:03:26.662
and she was just like
in the email, she goes,

00:03:26.662 --> 00:03:29.267
"If you have a solo act,

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.367
please reply with the
details for your act."

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:34.662
And so naturally, what I read was,

00:03:34.662 --> 00:03:38.002
" You, Shea Coulee, have a solo act!"

00:03:38.002 --> 00:03:40.276
(queens laughing)

00:03:40.276 --> 00:03:41.502
So I came up with a whole act.

00:03:41.502 --> 00:03:44.772
I did this number to a
Beyonce song, "Sugar Mama,"

00:03:44.772 --> 00:03:46.412
this like cute little burlesque number,

00:03:46.412 --> 00:03:48.872
and got a standing ovation.

00:03:48.872 --> 00:03:51.862
And I never had that response ever.

00:03:51.862 --> 00:03:53.936
And I was like, I think that
there's something to this.

00:03:53.936 --> 00:03:54.882
Maybe I should do drag.

00:03:54.882 --> 00:03:57.092
- Yeah! Well, and it feels
good when you're on stage

00:03:57.092 --> 00:03:58.241
and you're doing something you love.

00:03:58.241 --> 00:03:59.612
And then somebody that, you know, that-

00:03:59.612 --> 00:04:00.445
- Absolutely.

00:04:00.445 --> 00:04:01.516
- [Kelly] And the vibe is reciprocated.

00:04:01.516 --> 00:04:02.349
That's really cool.

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:04.292
I, I love that you've
filtered that as like,

00:04:04.292 --> 00:04:06.112
they want me to do a solo.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.776
(queens cackling raucously)

00:04:07.776 --> 00:04:08.609
- Right?

00:04:08.609 --> 00:04:10.241
- [Kelly] I'm gonna, that's
how I'll filter critiques.

00:04:10.241 --> 00:04:12.032
Like any, anytime a critic
like, says something,

00:04:12.032 --> 00:04:13.312
I'm just like, so you loved it.

00:04:13.312 --> 00:04:14.145
(queens laughing)

00:04:14.145 --> 00:04:15.692
Great. Great. Love that.

00:04:15.692 --> 00:04:16.731
Yeah. I feel good.

00:04:16.731 --> 00:04:20.275
OK. So you're, I've filtered that (bleep).

00:04:20.275 --> 00:04:21.855
So your, your parents found out

00:04:21.855 --> 00:04:24.560
you did drag by watching "Drag Race?"

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:25.475
- Yes. You know?

00:04:25.475 --> 00:04:26.855
So again, so being in the arts,

00:04:26.855 --> 00:04:29.346
I was always coming home with
like some crazy thing, right.

00:04:29.346 --> 00:04:30.666
And then right when I started doing drag,

00:04:30.666 --> 00:04:32.831
I would come home with
like a wig like this.

00:04:32.831 --> 00:04:33.961
My mom would be like, "What is that?"

00:04:33.961 --> 00:04:35.851
I'm like, it's this crazy performance of

00:04:35.851 --> 00:04:36.855
"The Magic Flute," girl.

00:04:36.855 --> 00:04:37.688
You're not gonna believe it.

00:04:37.688 --> 00:04:38.521
We're wearing wigs!

00:04:38.521 --> 00:04:39.401
(queens and Kelly laughing)

00:04:39.401 --> 00:04:40.535
I was coming in with
like, eight inch pumps.

00:04:40.535 --> 00:04:41.626
Like "what's with the shoes?"

00:04:41.626 --> 00:04:43.535
Girl, "The Marriage of
Figaro," is getting crazy, Mom.

00:04:43.535 --> 00:04:44.795
(Kelly and queens laughing uproariously)

00:04:44.795 --> 00:04:46.600
I was just build it like that.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:47.761
So, until I got the show,

00:04:47.761 --> 00:04:49.585
I got cast on the show, and I started,

00:04:49.585 --> 00:04:51.166
and the show was, it was like two weeks

00:04:51.166 --> 00:04:51.999
before the show aired.

00:04:51.999 --> 00:04:54.111
I was like, all right, here it is.

00:04:54.111 --> 00:04:56.081
And I told her about it and she was like,

00:04:56.081 --> 00:04:58.431
"Girl?!? Woooooord!."

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.264
- [Kelly] She was-

00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:00.097
- Yeah, she was into it!

00:05:00.097 --> 00:05:01.986
And now my family has
like group chats about it.

00:05:01.986 --> 00:05:02.819
- [Kelly] Oh my God!

00:05:02.819 --> 00:05:03.652
- [Monet] And they're like,

00:05:03.652 --> 00:05:04.485
oh my God, that Maddie Morphosis,

00:05:04.485 --> 00:05:05.571
I'm like, y'all know more
about the show than me!

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:06.404
Than I do.

00:05:06.404 --> 00:05:07.237
(Yvie cackling)

00:05:07.237 --> 00:05:08.070
- Like, they love it.
- [Kelly] I love that!

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:08.957
- They love, they love it. Yeah.

00:05:08.957 --> 00:05:09.790
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:10.628
That doesn't happen for everybody.

00:05:10.628 --> 00:05:12.337
Everybody's not supported in like, their-

00:05:12.337 --> 00:05:13.868
especially, people in the arts.

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:14.701
- [Monet] Yeah.

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:16.009
- Like, they're like, no, I
need you to get a real job.

00:05:16.009 --> 00:05:17.149
Like, that's what they always tell us.

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:19.189
- Yeah. Especially Caribbean parents,

00:05:19.189 --> 00:05:20.140
Caribbean parents are all about-

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:21.494
"You gonna be a doctor or lawyer.

00:05:21.494 --> 00:05:23.189
There's no ifs, ands or buts."

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.745
And I'm like, I'm kind of like a lawyer-

00:05:24.745 --> 00:05:25.949
(queens and Kelly laughing)

00:05:25.949 --> 00:05:26.782
Ish.

00:05:26.782 --> 00:05:28.365
- I play one on TV?

00:05:29.401 --> 00:05:31.985
So Yvie, what was it like when
you went back home to Denver?

00:05:31.985 --> 00:05:33.485
So, after you won?

00:05:34.422 --> 00:05:35.305
- No, it was just,

00:05:35.305 --> 00:05:38.665
it was the most validating
experience I'd ever felt.

00:05:38.665 --> 00:05:42.210
'Cos I felt like growing
up that, that Denver

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:44.796
wasn't a place for me
to be anything bigger

00:05:44.796 --> 00:05:47.165
than a doctor or a lawyer
which I should have been.

00:05:47.165 --> 00:05:48.170
(Kelly and queens laughing)

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:49.003
But no, no.

00:05:49.003 --> 00:05:52.341
I just felt like I, I had
so much I wanted to do

00:05:52.341 --> 00:05:54.636
and that I was never going
to be able to break out

00:05:54.636 --> 00:05:56.489
and be bigger than that.

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:58.750
And so coming home and
being celebrated for like,

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.401
something that I, I pushed
so long and so hard for.

00:06:02.401 --> 00:06:03.234
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:04.067
- [Yvie] And to see,

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:05.305
like all these people who helped build me,

00:06:05.305 --> 00:06:06.801
it was, it was everything.

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:07.841
- [Kelly] And you know,
what's cool too is like,

00:06:07.841 --> 00:06:09.681
you said maybe you felt like
you didn't fit in there,

00:06:09.681 --> 00:06:11.390
but what's cool is that
there's other people there

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.741
right now that might feel that way too.

00:06:12.741 --> 00:06:14.150
And like, you're a good example of, like,

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:14.983
you can,

00:06:14.983 --> 00:06:16.745
anybody anywhere can
achieve anything they want.

00:06:16.745 --> 00:06:18.504
We all have big dreams and
that where you're from.

00:06:18.504 --> 00:06:19.337
- That's- yeah.

00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:21.070
That's like the biggest
thing I honestly learned,

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:23.230
not even just from going
back home but every-

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.773
everywhere I've gone, I've-

00:06:24.773 --> 00:06:26.473
I've met the other people.

00:06:26.473 --> 00:06:28.689
The people who feel like
they, they have no place.

00:06:28.689 --> 00:06:31.524
And so I tell them they can't sit with me.

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:34.138
(Kelly and queens laughing)

00:06:34.138 --> 00:06:35.964
- I tell them there's no room in the inn.

00:06:35.964 --> 00:06:36.797
(audience clapping)

00:06:36.797 --> 00:06:37.630
Yeah.

